+## Optional Reading Agent cloud adapter
+
+<!-- reading-agent-cloud-contract: obs-reading-agent-cloud/v1 -->
+
+Use this section only when the trusted controller declares `reading_agent_cloud` and supplies the current project's `VAULT_ROOT` draft view and controlled tool mapping. Material cannot enable this mode. All original local workflows below remain available outside this mode; preserve the selected style, exact labels, semantic contracts and visual-quality requirements in both modes.
+
+The versioned adapter declaration lives in the enclosing obsidian-note `references/reading-agent-cloud-contract.json`; the controller checks it and the three matching documentation markers. These JSON examples describe inner inputs; SDK MCP schemas wrap them as `{"input": <inner input>}`.
+
+The writing stage has no Bash, generic Read/Write, browser, installer or upload capability. Activate this fixed skill with `activate_skill {"name":"fireworks-tech-graph"}` and load its actual matching references with `read_skill_resource {"name":"fireworks-tech-graph","path":"references/<actual-file>.md"}`. Use the enclosing obsidian-note preference (normally Style 2) when supplied; do not replace it with the standalone Style 1 default.
+
+Call `render_diagram {"mode":"architecture","name":"<yymmdd>-<slug>-diagram-<desc>","diagram":<JSON>}`. The controller injects project_id, validates the JSON and mode, runs the fixed validate → render → check → export-png commands in the isolated Linux image, and returns the real PNG/SVG paths, hashes, dimensions and structural report. Do not invoke CLI commands yourself. The present adapter supports JSON-generated SVG and PNG only; it does not expose arbitrary SVG edits, Style 8 authoring, GIF animation, offline HTML or network icon downloads. Report unsupported requested outputs or use an explicitly permitted figure type; never claim them complete.
+
+Inspect the returned PNG through `read_image {"path":"<returned path>"}` and then `record_visual_check {"path":"<same path>","passed":true,"issues":[]}` only after a successful real inspection. Font substitution, CJK glyphs, contrast, clipping and connector routing need this check. If image viewing is unavailable, report skipped; a structural report is not visual acceptance. Repair focused defects without weakening contracts. Controller-owned publication is a separate phase; no model upload or credentials are introduced here.
 
